Check the chmod mode before looking at any file.
chmod parsed MODE only for a file it had found, so with no existing
file an invalid MODE went unreported, and only the missing files were.
Check MODE once at the start, as coreutils does, and report it before
anything else.

---
 coreutils/chmod.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/chmod.c
+++ b/coreutils/chmod.c
@@ -136,6 +136,9 @@
 
 	/* Ok, ready to do the deed now */
 	smode = *argv++;
+	/* Whether MODE is valid doesn't depend on the file's mode */
+	if (bb_parse_mode(smode, 0) < 0)
+		bb_error_msg_and_die("invalid mode '%s'", smode);
 	do {
 		if (!recursive_action(*argv,
 			OPT_RECURSE,    // recurse
